{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788294475,"nonce":"MuOVkr82YXFqt50bGN6Wt9vqlwU=","message":"BULLET 4's BYTE-IDENTICAL-SAVE HALF IS RUN, AND IT PASSES HARDER THAN ASKED. This is the check `accept/3.5-dialog-verbs.py` prints as a NOTE at 1.2c — \"the ORCHESTRATOR's to run: save, `quests`, `quest` on every id, save again, diff the `\u003cquests\u003e` region. This script cannot save without perturbing the very counters it is checking.\"\n\nRun 2026-09-01 on `_RimWorld-Agent` session `20260901T195344`, assembly `1.0.0+094b14a`, on a colony carrying **9 quests** (4 available / 4 ongoing / 1 ended, 3 with an outstanding choice).\n\nProcedure:\n\n1. `journal-selftest {steps:[\"save\"], save_name:\"qobs-A\"}` — `GameDataSaveLoader.SaveGame`, no other step.\n2. `quest {id}` for every one of ids 0..8, then `quests {cap:50}`.\n3. `journal-selftest {steps:[\"save\"], save_name:\"qobs-B\"}`.\n4. Diff.\n\nResult:\n\n- `\u003cquests\u003e` region: **168,043 bytes, identical.**\n- And the check the acceptance did not ask for: **the ENTIRE 15,401,531-byte save is byte-identical.** `sha256 b5a2f9d4adceaa007fedae9b812da8713397ec29aa81c06a86421ff9d6087e11` for both files. Not just the quest region — nothing anywhere in the game state moved.\n\nThat is the strongest form of \"observers never mutate\" available: ten quest reads over a nine-quest log, including three with unresolved `QuestPart_Choice`, and the serialized world is bit-for-bit what it was.\n\nA NOTE on method for anyone repeating it: **`journal-selftest`'s step list is `steps` (a StrList) and NOT `kind`.** Passing `kind:\"save\"` is silently ignored and the verb runs its DEFAULT list — `[\"letter\",\"message\",\"error\",\"downed\",\"break\"]` — which downs a colonist, sends another berserk and logs a red error. I did that four times before noticing. Filed as measured evidence on `7382bdd`.","files":null}]}